BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (negative receipts. Store integer cents and integer basis points, with explicit half-up fee rounding. The natural) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (claim key combines client, invoice item, and play; make invoice_key granular enough to distinguish) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (recoverable line items while preventing the same line from being counted twice under renamed campaigns.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (SHA-256 connects the database to immutable evidence retained outside it. A hash proves identity of bytes,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (not commercial validity, so a named reviewer still validates every document. The scoring script records facts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (without granting credentials. Run intake with a JSON payload containing the documented parameters;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (missing facts, altered replay payloads, or duplicate natural keys fail instead of silently changing an existing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (claim.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (Every mutating function obtains BEGIN IMMEDIATE before reading mutable state, holds the SQLite writer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (reservation through validation and posting, and commits the event with its business effect. Unique event) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (identifiers reject changed retries; a matching replay returns without another posting. A partial unique index) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (allows one earnings entry per claim, and a provider-qualified external reference prevents two local claims) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (from sharing one acknowledgement. Concurrent receipts serialize before checking the open balance, so two) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (workers cannot each consume the same receivable. These properties remove check-then-write races within) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (this controlled database path. Use one local database on durable storage, not a network filesystem or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (independent copied databases. Set foreign keys on every connection, retain FULL synchronous durability,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (and restrict write access to the service identity. The reference makes no network submissions: it records an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (acknowledgement only after a documented external action. Where a provider supports idempotency keys,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (reuse a stable claim identifier. Where it does not, an ambiguous timeout requires a status inquiry and human) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (resolution, never an automatic resend. A database transaction cannot make an unrelated carrier system) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (participate in an atomic commit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (The verification and escrow state machine starts at held, advances through verified, submitted, settled, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (invoiced, and allows documented voiding before settlement. Here escrow means an internal evidence hold,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (not possession of client money. Submission requires a provider-qualified acknowledgement; settlement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (requires documentary proof that the actual customer recovery equals the reviewed amount. A partial award) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (stops the transition for controlled rework rather than overstating fees. Invoicing records completed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (contractual performance and an unconditional fee right, then debits fee receivables and credits operator) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (revenue atomically. Bank receipts debit cash and credit those receivables using an account-qualified bank) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (transaction identifier. The minimal implementation allocates one bank transaction to one claim; multi-invoice) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (deposits need a dedicated allocation model before use. Reconciliation shows earned fees minus allocated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm (receipts equals remaining receivables for every claim and cohort. QA runs inside one read transaction,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.02 Tm (avoiding inconsistent snapshots during concurrent writes. Structural checks supplement, rather than replace,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.80 Tm (independent bank and source-document matching. Export monthly operator expenses into the accounting) Tj ET
